.SH NAME
.PP
jeopardy.engine \(en Jeopardy game rules as a state machine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
from jeopardy.engine import Engine, ActionError
.PD 0
.P
.PD
.PD 0
.P
.PD
\f[B]Engine\f[R](\f[I]game\f[R]=None, \f[I]on_log\f[R]=None)
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]Engine\f[R] applies player actions to a \f[B]Game\f[R] (see
\f[B]jeopardy\-model\f[R](3)) and enforces the rules.
It does no I/O and never reads a clock: methods that depend on time take
\f[I]now\f[R] in seconds from the caller.
This keeps it easy to test, and lets \f[B]jeopardy\-server\f[R](1) be
the only place that talks to the network.
.PP
Every action takes the id of the player making it, \f[I]pid\f[R], as its
first argument.
An action that is not allowed in the current phase, or not by that
player, raises \f[B]ActionError\f[R] with a short message and changes
nothing.
.PP
\f[I]game\f[R] is an existing \f[B]Game\f[R] to resume, or None for a
new one.
\f[I]on_log\f[R] is called with each game event as it is logged.
The last 50 events are also kept in \f[B]game.log\f[R].
.SH METHODS
Lobby
.TP
\f[B]join\f[R](\f[I]pid\f[R], \f[I]name\f[R], \f[I]host\f[R]=False)
Add a player, or mark a known one as connected again.
Fails if the name is taken, ignoring case, or if \f[I]host\f[R] is true
and there is already a host.
.TP
\f[B]disconnect\f[R](\f[I]pid\f[R])
Mark a player as not connected.
Their seat and score are kept.
.TP
\f[B]start\f[R](\f[I]pid\f[R], \f[I]qs\f[R])
Host only.
Load a \f[B]QuestionSet\f[R] and start the game.
Needs at least one player besides the host.
The first player to have joined gets control.
.TP
\f[B]reset\f[R](\f[I]pid\f[R])
Host only.
Return to the lobby with the same people and scores set to zero.
.PP
Board
.TP
\f[B]select_clue\f[R](\f[I]pid\f[R], \f[I]cat\f[R], \f[I]idx\f[R])
The player in control, or the host, picks a clue.
A Daily Double goes to the wager phase and any other clue is shown.
.TP
\f[B]skip_clue\f[R](\f[I]pid\f[R])
Host only.
Drop the open clue and reveal its answer.
.TP
\f[B]adjust_score\f[R](\f[I]pid\f[R], \f[I]target\f[R], \f[I]delta\f[R])
Host only.
Add \f[I]delta\f[R] to a player\(cqs score.
.PP
Daily Double
.TP
\f[B]set_wager\f[R](\f[I]pid\f[R], \f[I]amount\f[R])
The player in control wagers from 5 up to
\f[B]max_wager\f[R](\f[I]pid\f[R]), which is their score or the highest
value on the board, whichever is larger.
.PP
Buzzing
.TP
\f[B]open_buzzers\f[R](\f[I]pid\f[R], \f[I]now\f[R])
Host only.
Let players buzz in.
.TP
\f[B]buzz\f[R](\f[I]pid\f[R], \f[I]now\f[R])
A player tries to take the floor.
Returns True if they got it.
Buzzing before the buzzers open locks the player out for a quarter of a
second.
A player who has already answered the clue wrongly cannot buzz again.
.TP
\f[B]judge\f[R](\f[I]pid\f[R], \f[I]correct\f[R])
Host only.
A correct answer adds the clue\(cqs value, or the wager, to the score
and gives the player control.
A wrong one subtracts it and lets the others buzz.
The clue ends when someone is correct, when every player has tried, or
at once after a wrong Daily Double.
.PP
Final Jeopardy
.TP
\f[B]start_final\f[R](\f[I]pid\f[R])
Host only, from the board.
Only players with a positive score take part.
If there are none, the game is over.
.TP
\f[B]final_wager\f[R](\f[I]pid\f[R], \f[I]amount\f[R]), \f[B]final_answer\f[R](\f[I]pid\f[R], \f[I]text\f[R])
An eligible player wagers from 0 up to their score, then answers.
The phase moves on once everyone eligible has done so.
.TP
\f[B]force_advance\f[R](\f[I]pid\f[R])
Host only.
Move on without waiting.
Missing wagers become 0 and missing answers become \(lq(no answer)\(rq.
.TP
\f[B]judge_final\f[R](\f[I]pid\f[R], \f[I]target\f[R], \f[I]correct\f[R])
Host only.
Add or subtract the player\(cqs wager.
The game ends after the last player is judged.
.PP
Queries
.TP
\f[B]snapshot\f[R](\f[I]viewer\f[R])
The game as a JSON\-ready dictionary for one viewer, with hidden
information removed.
See \f[B]jeopardy\-protocol\f[R](7).
.TP
\f[B]current_clue\f[R](), \f[B]contestants\f[R](), \f[B]final_eligible\f[R](), \f[B]max_wager\f[R](\f[I]pid\f[R]), \f[B]max_board_value\f[R]()
Helpers that read the state.
